{"timestamp":"2026-04-24T11:25:45.113Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"Yes, `explain` does fetch metadata itself.\n\nIn particular:\n- It first tries tree-only fetches via [`FetchMetadataTreeOnly`](/home/coder/git/entireio/cli-sign/cmd/entire/cli/git_operations.go:411) and [`FetchV2MainTreeOnly`](/home/coder/git/entireio/cli-sign/cmd/entire/cli/git_operations.go:465).\n- If that is not enough, it falls back to the “full” fetch helpers in [`explain.go`](/home/coder/git/entireio/cli-sign/cmd/entire/cli/explain.go:494), which now also became shallow because of your change.\n\nSo yes, `explain` could be made to unshallow or use a non-shallow fetch for its author-lookup path. That would likely fix the first issue I listed.\n\nIt would not fix the second issue.\n\nThe bigger compatibility problem is that the shared metadata fetch helpers now seed local refs shallowly:\n- v1 via [`FetchMetadataBranch`](/home/coder/git/entireio/cli-sign/cmd/entire/cli/git_operations.go:403)\n- v2 via [`FetchV2MainRef`](/home/coder/git/entireio/cli-sign/cmd/entire/cli/git_operations.go:472)\n- checkpoint-remote via [`strategy.FetchMetadataBranch`](/home/coder/git/entireio/cli-sign/cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_remote.go:118)\n\nThose refs are later advanced through [`SafelyAdvanceLocalRef`](/home/coder/git/entireio/cli-sign/cmd/entire/cli/strategy/common.go:139), whose logic explicitly assumes the existing local ref has full history. Once a local metadata ref is shallow, that assumption is false for every workflow, not just `explain`.\n\nSo:\n- `explain` can be patched locally by unshallowing or using a non-shallow fetch when it needs history.\n- But that is only a partial fix.\n- The shared helper change is still unsafe because it changes the long-term shape of the local metadata refs and can break later safety checks.\n\nIf you want the low-risk version, the right split is:\n- Keep tree-only helpers shallow.\n- Keep blob-by-hash as-is.\n- Revert the shared “full metadata fetch” helpers back to non-shallow.\n- If desired, optimize `explain` separately with a targeted unshallow/history fetch only when author lookup actually needs it.","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
